      "en": "- Unit Hello is for settling in, school familiarity, and early participation, not formal teaching.\n- Children are not required to complete worksheets, answer open questions, sing full songs, speak in complete sentences, or perform for assessment.\n- Separation, participation, and group joining should remain gentle and emotionally safe.\n- Watching, staying close, needing comfort, joining briefly, choosing one object, or taking one helper turn can all be appropriate PK responses.\n- Optional Challenge language is readiness-based and must not become a whole-class mastery target.",
